    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_974e52ea6820e1a5eed17a2306b08941940e284f83156fc017d8430867989992",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After contour algebra isolates the main terms, both the weighted zero-displacement formula and the unweighted zero-count formula leave phase data as the live error channel. The available RH estimates then make arg G_k, rather than further main-term manipulation, the source's limiting quantitative input for N_k(T).",
